<title>UK: UK's Ionica to create up to 600 new jobs.</title>
<headline>UK's Ionica to create up to 600 new jobs.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ionica Plc, the fledgling UK telephone company based on wireless technology, said on Wednesday it planned to create up to 600 new jobs at a new customer call centre in Birmingham, central England.</p>
<p>Ionica, which delivers its telecoms services via radio waves to antennae on houses, said the call centre, its second, would open for business in mid-1997.</p>
<p>Ionica, partly-owned by Yorkshire Electricity Plc and Northern Electric Plc, has a national licence and plans to cover three-quarters of homes in England and Wales by 2000.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
</text>
